<title>JAPAN: Copper trader Hamanaka faces Tokyo court this week.</title>
<headline>Copper trader Hamanaka faces Tokyo court this week.</headline>
<byline>Eiichiro Tokumoto</byline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>One-time copper market king Yasuo Hamanaka goes on trial on Monday, charged with defrauding his company with unauthorised trades that created losses of $2.6 billion.</p>
<p>The case, the biggest financial fraud in history, has raised questions of how one person could have amassed such losses without anyone's knowledge and whether Japan properly scrutinises its financial sector.</p>
</text>
